    "id": 205345632,
    "iid": 15,
    "project_id": 86882182,
    "title": "An object with no prototype leaks its arcane mark when freed",
    "description": "## Problem\n\n`free_obj()` (`src/core/db.c`) frees an object's strings in one of two ways. An object with a\nprototype goes through `free_object_strings_proto()`, which frees `arcane_mark`. An object with\nno prototype (`GET_OBJ_RNUM(obj) == NOWHERE`) goes through `free_object_strings()`\n(`src/olc/genobj.c`), which frees `name`, `description`, `short_description`,\n`action_description`, the extra descriptions, `char_sdesc` and `restring_identifier`, but not\n`arcane_mark`.\n\nSo an object with no prototype that carries an arcane mark leaks the mark when it is extracted.\nThe mark is set with `strdup()` when a saved record with an `AMrk` line loads\n(`src/obj/objsave.c`, both parsers) and in `copy_object()` (`src/olc/genobj.c`).\n\n## Evidence\n\nRead from the code, not measured. The existing test\n`Test_object_saves_bind_player_house_and_serialized_text` frees the mark by hand before\n`extract_obj()` for this reason.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nFree `arcane_mark` in `free_object_strings()`, after checking its other callers (the OLC cleanup\nand the prototype teardown in `destroy_db()`) so that no path frees it twice.\n\nFound on 2026-10-04 while writing the S13 tests (work item #13); it is not part of that work.",
    "state": "closed",
