    "id": 205367658,
    "iid": 17,
    "project_id": 86882182,
    "title": "A loaded sheath loses its weapons on a pet and leaks them when extracted",
    "description": "**Defect.** A sheath's weapons hang off the sheath object (`sheath_primary`, `sheath_secondary`) and are handled only by the player save and by `sheath` / `unsheath`. Two paths lose track of them.\n\n1. **Pet saves.** `objsave_save_obj_record_db_pet()` writes no sheath rows. A loaded sheath given to a pet comes back empty when the pet is restored, and its weapons are in no row.\n2. **Extraction.** `extract_obj()` does not look at a sheath's weapons. Extracting a loaded sheath (junk, a shop sale, the extraction after a rent save) frees the sheath and leaves the weapons in `object_list` with no holder. After a rent save that is a memory leak only, since the rows were written. After a junk or a sale the weapons are gone from play without having been destroyed.\n\n**Not part of this.** A loaded sheath lying in a house: MR !20 (review P1) made the house save store its weapons as the house's own objects.\n\n**Fix.** Give the pet writer the sheath rows the player writer has (or refuse a loaded sheath on a pet), and make `extract_obj()` extract what a sheath holds.\n\nFound while fixing the review of MR !20 (S13); read from the code, not played. Not changed there.",
    "state": "closed",
    "created_at": "2026-10-04T08:02:19.310Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-08T06:39:19.712Z",
